# SPACE FACTORY — Use Lore Research

Before proposing or implementing ideas that affect **tone, atmosphere, narrative, enemy/hive fantasy, factory pressure, environmental storytelling, audio/visual mood, comps, or asset choices**, read the lore corpus first.

## Required reading order (keep it light)

1. `lore/BIBLE.md` — living canon (prefer this over raw digests)
2. `lore/INDEX.md` — active thematic pillars and last research run
3. `lore/README.md` — north star + folder layout
4. Latest `lore/YYYY-MM-DD/summary.md` — headline takeaways / unabsorbed candidates
5. Deeper files only as needed: `articles.md`, `videos.md`, `reviews-comps.md`, `stories.md`, `assets-tools.md`
6. `lore/wishlist-paywalled.md` — before recommending paid assets/tools

If the bible’s **Last absorbed research** is older than the newest digest, run `/lore-bible` before design work or `/lore-gap`.

## How to use it

- Prefer bible pillars and motifs (workplace-as-trap, biomass using ship systems, factory-tied threat, lonely industrial dread) over generic sci-fi or cozy factory tropes.
- Cite which bible section or lore note shaped a suggestion when it materially changes design or art direction.
- Strong new ideas → promote via `/lore-bible` (canon or Open experiments), not by editing digests into pseudo-canon.
- Do **not** paste copyrighted fiction into the game; use motif/summary notes and original writing.
- Do **not** buy paywalled assets; point at the wishlist.
- After updating `wishlist-paywalled.md` or free leads in any `assets-tools.md`, run `lore/sync-assets-sheet.ps1` so `lore/assets-wishlist.csv` stays in sync for the Google Sheet (`lore/GOOGLE-SHEET.md`).
- Pure mechanical bugfixes with no mood/design impact may skip lore.

## Game identity (do not drift)

Horror-infused **factory management** on a broken far-future ship under hive-alien pressure. Tone: sad, lonely, fear. Factory layout is primary; defense disrupts without replacing the loop. Story secondary to atmosphere and systems.

## Autonomous cycle (when improving the game from lore)

Use `/lore-bible` → `/lore-gap` → `/auto-dev` → `/bug-pass` against `BACKLOG.md` (see `AGENTS.md`). Skip `/lore-bible` only when the bible is already current with the latest digest. `SPACE FACTORY INFO/` is living design — beneficial changes allowed; keep docs in sync. Until `BACKLOG.md` Asset pack status is purchased, prefer work that needs no paid pack.

## Lore git policy

Commit lore research updates directly to `main`. Do not create `lore/daily-*` branches.

Daily cloud runs must remind the owner to sync locally — add a **Local sync** section to that day's `summary.md` and to `lore/INDEX.md` with `git pull origin main` (cwd: `D:\new project\SPACE FACTORY`).
